  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship)\n(section) Sec.2 in Draft / Sec.1 in Chaptered, amends TCA 2-2-141(a)\n(quote) The coordinator of elections shall compare the statewide voter registration database with the department of safety database to ensure non-United States citizens are not registered to vote in this state.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) Draft Sec.1, amends TCA 2-2-106(c)(1)(D) (removed by HA0815; not in Chaptered)\n(quote) The coordinator of elections shall compare the statewide voter registration database with those of other relevant state agencies and county records for this purpose; and\n(other) Draft Sec.1: makes the 2-2-106(c)(1)(D) comparison of registration addresses with other state agency and county records mandatory ('shall' instead of 'may'). This is an address check, not a citizenship check.\n(other) Draft Sec.2 / Chaptered Sec.1: changes 'may' to 'shall' in the 2-2-141(a) department-of-safety comparison that checks the voter list for non-citizens.\n(other) Last section: effective on becoming law (HA0409 would have made it July 1, 2024; it was withdrawn).\n(other) version: Draft 2670928 (Richey; SB 137 companion): carries slot d (Sec.2) and slot e (Sec.1 address comparison).\n(other) version: HA0409 (House Local Government amendment 1): changes the effective date to July 1, 2024 only; no ID/citizenship text; withdrawn on 2024-04-04.\n(other) version: HA0815 (House Local Government amendment 2): full rewrite keeping only the 2-2-141(a) 'shall compare' change (slot d) and dropping the 2-2-106 section; adopted 2024-04-04 per the action line (skeleton flag adopted=0).\n(other) version: Chaptered 2996207 (Pub. Ch. 900): equals the HA0815 text (2-2-141(a) only); same text as SB 137 Chaptered.\n(other) note: Mandatory 'shall compare' is an automatic database check of the voter list against department of safety records; the text puts no duty on voters to show citizenship proof. The same Public Chapter is listed under SB 137.\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
